    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Three meta-analyses have been conducted to provide synthesized evidence on the effectiveness of pharmacological interventions for depressive symptoms following stroke, but results were mixed... With mixed conclusions, the effectiveness of pharmacological interventions for post-stroke depressive symptoms has not yet been determined.",
      "reason": "The introduction describes current knowledge, including mixed results of pharmacological meta-analyses and existing qualitative NPI reviews, identifying the uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "For these reasons, an alternative, or addition, to pharmaceutical options is essential to ensure effective management of depressive symptoms after stroke... Therefore, to address this research gap, this study aimed to conduct a meta-analysis to synthesize and compare the available evidence regarding the effectiveness of various NPIs for treating depression in people following stroke.",
      "reason": "The need and importance of the review are explicitly explained, citing unaddressed depression consequences, limitations of pharmacological options, and the research gap."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Three reviews have identified several NPIs for post-stroke depression and have qualitatively provided evidence. 8,11,14 However, none of these reviews quantitatively demonstrated the effectiveness of different types of NPIs.",
      "reason": "Existing similar reviews are identified and cited, and the need for the current quantitative review is explained."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "NPIs, which are defined as science-based and non-invasive interventions on human health, may provide an alternative to ameliorate depressive symptoms. Several NPIs for depression exist, such as complementary and alternative therapy (CAT), exercise, psychosocial therapy, non-invasive cranial stimulation, and multifactorial behavioral treatment.",
      "reason": "The rationale for NPIs as an alternative is given and intervention types are listed, but no explicit mechanism of action for the interventions is described."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No logic model or description of hypothesized relationships between intervention components and outcomes is reported in the retrieved evidence."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 88
}

